[{:db/id "q-135310/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ad117072-e02c-57ec-a98f-4c3d21553667" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135310/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "4d461c17-b58e-5023-8c3a-c2ad4253b2be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135310/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "15bf75da-16aa-5633-bbeb-7a69b38b6e68" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135310/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "58c124eb-7990-5a51-a5d8-775a785f8439" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135310/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "59c8d70e-ba02-5735-ae76-a4555a62fb3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135310/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "789ae930-bd06-5d6e-9597-e5a1beb87c1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135310/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-135310/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-135310/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-135310/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-135310/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-135310/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135310" :question/id #uuid "f14c2161-b221-51e8-9068-326a4f843d68" :question/math-academy-id "q-135310" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.3 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.3 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.4 & 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ \\frac{4}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- $Pq=q$\n- $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.3 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.3 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.4 & 0.3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ \\frac{4}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1.2}{9}+\\frac{0.5}{9} \\\\ \\frac{0.6}{9}+\\frac{1.2}{9}+\\frac{0.2}{9} \\\\ \\frac{2.4}{9}+\\frac{1.6}{9}+\\frac{0.3}{9}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.7}{9} \\\\ \\frac{2}{9} \\\\ \\frac{4.3}{9}\\end{aligned}]\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135310/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135310"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135306/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "44511b43-37e7-5a09-80e6-03886e9d2300" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135306/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "1637b7cc-7816-5b20-ab20-fd3ec2553619" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135306/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0da29330-97e8-5c08-a5b9-e926862ea06e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135306/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "996354da-ffa1-5f66-825e-85c1fc82506e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135306/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0517cfb1-d16a-5115-b237-68ca90f4652d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135306/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "83cc77b2-be86-5143-9d4f-fe8f63aa2909" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135306/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-135306/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-135306/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-135306/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-135306/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-135306/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135306" :question/id #uuid "224b3ef2-275a-5b9b-8943-2770e7619fc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-135306" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.85\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- $Pq=q$\n- $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.85\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.4}{7}+\\frac{0.6}{7} \\\\ \\frac{0.6}{7}+\\frac{3.4}{7}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}]=q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector such that $Pq=q.$ So, it's a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-135306/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135306"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135311/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d689dc5d-6fab-558f-ab85-e04cf8370ee1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135311/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "8d1447be-964c-502c-8c2b-8636dc6c2f7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135311/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "a600d558-c1f7-5011-b7e5-7dcde2682dd9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135311/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "bef183b8-2db6-56f1-ac95-f87f184c696f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135311/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "409dba80-03f0-5d5a-81bb-bc02d4266b94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135311/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c9abf1c-6664-5535-9fcf-917573dbb6cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135311/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-135311/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-135311/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-135311/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-135311/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-135311/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135311" :question/id #uuid "356faffb-7793-5fb7-ac0b-96c95b3bd6a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-135311" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.15 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.7 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.15 & 0.05\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- $Pq=q$\n- $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.15 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.7 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.15 & 0.05\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.03+0.105+0.12 \\\\ 0.06+0.49+0.07 \\\\ 0.01+0.105+0.01\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.255 \\\\ 0.62 \\\\ 0.125\\end{aligned}]\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135311/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135311"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-110189"] :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15} \\\\ \\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- $Pq=q$\n- $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15} \\\\ \\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.4}{15}+\\frac{5.6}{15} \\\\ \\frac{5.6}{15}+\\frac{2.4}{15}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15} \\\\ \\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}]=q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector such that $Pq=q.$ So, it's a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-110239"] :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0.5 \\\\ 1 & 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- $Pq=q$\n- $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0.5 \\\\ 1 & 0.5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0+\\frac{1.5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1.5}{4}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8}\\end{aligned}]\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-135325/selection/c4f2d0cddc9dea7da08df1a75b0eebc8f3ffe495dfe56aac169e840a5523a6f2" :answer/id #uuid "92e8220f-7ede-5531-90cd-1d34a4c38dce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135325/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" :answer/id #uuid "76880b0d-414c-5a4d-a217-7d8835529d71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135325/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer/id #uuid "e34f64bb-1040-583b-b296-6e5ec8befb10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135325/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "c67851d5-a3dc-5b49-8194-6ed059e0f57f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135325/selection/f83734f398ed62d6a50cc8a97c78185beac5115da55d97e043b0491039006ab6" :answer/id #uuid "051716d7-e0b8-583c-a9e2-7686a7203dff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135325/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbf77d19-a620-5f4c-b2c3-617769595dd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135325/selection/f83734f398ed62d6a50cc8a97c78185beac5115da55d97e043b0491039006ab6" :answer-field/choices ["q-135325/selection/c4f2d0cddc9dea7da08df1a75b0eebc8f3ffe495dfe56aac169e840a5523a6f2" "q-135325/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" "q-135325/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" "q-135325/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-135325/selection/f83734f398ed62d6a50cc8a97c78185beac5115da55d97e043b0491039006ab6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135325" :question/id #uuid "4fea3684-1d6a-5826-a4b9-83e705fd159c" :question/math-academy-id "q-135325" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0.3 \\\\ 1 & 0.7\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $q$ is the steady-state vector of the stochastic matrix $P,$ what is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq & =q \\\\ Pq-q & =0 \\\\ Pq-Iq & =0 \\\\ (P-I)q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0.3 \\\\ 1 & 0.7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0.3 \\\\ 1 & -0.3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0.3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -0.3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0.3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+0.3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 10{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{3}{10}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{10}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{10}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{13}{10}{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =\\frac{10}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{13} \\\\ \\frac{10}{13}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a-b=\\frac{3}{13}-\\frac{10}{13}=-\\frac{7}{13}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-135325/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f53fa522-6d50-51d9-abdd-62735575a2d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135325"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135408/selection/cbb6f4ecb9b5353f428fa6553193da37c4b392bd7aaabe99ba7486c166d9ef2f" :answer/id #uuid "47abbc21-177f-5903-a443-c433e6b97303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135408/selection/16da0ae14727e3199a8662e284117784a91c2f076e6dc6914081f8c0e500d923" :answer/id #uuid "be0a8077-3b4f-58c5-b172-9dc75ca6a046" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "62\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135408/selection/aef8669f54d004acc9e3a6b0d942a949a71408430406851d11769f9b3fe5f442" :answer/id #uuid "f09fd2c2-f4f5-5264-9bed-c09048ffa335" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135408/selection/ff497df650bf94fafcc6873af7d0104f8d5bb6ff89b5f46371b7510501d19717" :answer/id #uuid "e21eea60-096d-5129-9df6-8af9d44aa77c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135408/selection/fa10a46d9573ab071d2d907e138d9e345712888f3fa9134e68816f20eff4765a" :answer/id #uuid "e981bcfb-3dbc-525c-a92d-e8c2dfe5d85c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135408/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa075338-57bf-5f22-9c69-021fcc95c24e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135408/selection/aef8669f54d004acc9e3a6b0d942a949a71408430406851d11769f9b3fe5f442" :answer-field/choices ["q-135408/selection/cbb6f4ecb9b5353f428fa6553193da37c4b392bd7aaabe99ba7486c166d9ef2f" "q-135408/selection/16da0ae14727e3199a8662e284117784a91c2f076e6dc6914081f8c0e500d923" "q-135408/selection/aef8669f54d004acc9e3a6b0d942a949a71408430406851d11769f9b3fe5f442" "q-135408/selection/ff497df650bf94fafcc6873af7d0104f8d5bb6ff89b5f46371b7510501d19717" "q-135408/selection/fa10a46d9573ab071d2d907e138d9e345712888f3fa9134e68816f20eff4765a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135408" :question/id #uuid "05a39ded-7d7a-5e3b-b1de-693f0bc3abbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-135408" :question/problem "There are two groups of people In a small town: those who travel to work by car and those who travel by train. Every year a study is done in which people are asked about their preference between using trains versus cars. The table below shows the results of this study.\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Car** | **Train** |\n| To: | **Car** | $0.35$ | $0.25$ |\n| **Train** | $0.65$ | $0.75$ |  |\n\nIt's found that $65%$ of people who currently travel by car will switch to train next year, while $25%$ of people who currently travel by train will switch to their car next year.\n\nAssuming that the town has $90\\,000$ people that travel to work by train or car, and the given probabilities remain constant over many years, how many people will eventually use the train to travel to work?" :question/worked-solution "From the table, we get the corresponding stochastic matrix \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.35 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.65 & 0.75\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that $P$ contains only positive entries. So, the matrix $P$ is regular. As a result, after many years, the distribution will eventually converge to the unique steady-state vector of $P,$ and this convergence does not depend on the initial state.\n\nRecall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq=q\\,⟹\\,(P-I)q=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.35 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.65 & 0.75\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.65 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.65 & -0.25\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.65 & 0.25 & 0 \\\\ 0.65 & -0.25 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-0.65 & 0.25 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{13}{x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{13}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{13}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{18}{13}{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =\\frac{13}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{18} \\\\ \\frac{13}{18}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{13}{18}$ of the people will eventually use the train to travel. Therefore, the number of people who will eventually use the train is\n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{18}\\cdot 90\\,000=65\\,000.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135408/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f53fa522-6d50-51d9-abdd-62735575a2d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135408"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-110242"] :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.9\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $q$ is the steady-state vector of the stochastic matrix $P,$ what is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq & =q \\\\ Pq-q & =0 \\\\ Pq-Iq & =0 \\\\ (P-I)q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.6 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.6 & -0.1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.6 & 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0.6 & -0.1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-0.6 & 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{6}{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{6}{7}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a-b=\\frac{1}{7}-\\frac{6}{7}=-\\frac{5}{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-135323/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "2d0b87a9-d299-5a56-8a6a-22d820d2115e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135323/selection/fcc08b5493ae6f7b4bc0aad6b1791b974d36d4679ce4f932434b29e95cebea06" :answer/id #uuid "58b382ab-a56a-5b49-8e9d-787ae8352859" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135323/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer/id #uuid "6df85110-15fd-505e-b5ac-92393d37976c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135323/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "77063f55-06e8-542e-9b7a-8b8342e80dfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135323/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "347fcef8-781e-572f-806b-5dd979ef962c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135323/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b693fe4e-03e4-5e8c-b592-73edca9a4053" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135323/selection/fcc08b5493ae6f7b4bc0aad6b1791b974d36d4679ce4f932434b29e95cebea06" :answer-field/choices ["q-135323/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-135323/selection/fcc08b5493ae6f7b4bc0aad6b1791b974d36d4679ce4f932434b29e95cebea06" "q-135323/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" "q-135323/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-135323/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135323" :question/id #uuid "696e69c1-aaed-5b30-adfb-2c3b0b8df1c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-135323" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.4\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $q$ is the steady-state vector of the stochastic matrix $P,$ what is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq & =q \\\\ Pq-q & =0 \\\\ Pq-Iq & =0 \\\\ (P-I)q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.75 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.75 & -0.6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.75 & 0.6 & 0 \\\\ 0.75 & -0.6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-0.75 & 0.6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-0.75{x}_{1}+0.6{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 75{x}_{1}-60{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{5}{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ \\frac{5}{9}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a-b=\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{5}{9}=-\\frac{1}{9}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-135323/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f53fa522-6d50-51d9-abdd-62735575a2d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135323"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135330/selection/d9419fe7cabdc7d4a05eed4347f4c93c371a5fc839025fe3b05d90b4f2cc11c3" :answer/id #uuid "e2fc5908-16df-54ed-a2a1-a17730f52f09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135330/selection/3b526d0871203a7fa20c2a891525c650a26e23eb2a93fea36737a1cf4d4423af" :answer/id #uuid "47353adb-d497-5fa5-a49e-7681b857860c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135330/selection/583ed5a6da69542ecec5bee151e2915afa46c47d13c8442b64a6497084c99e78" :answer/id #uuid "0c3182ae-4d4d-5e84-ad0e-0280dc50dc2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{33}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135330/selection/bf254af2a78e33a4bd565e51e6fc486096a404668e6dc60947f3560e2e649954" :answer/id #uuid "b80213a9-50e7-52a8-9b78-68b1fb760d15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{33}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135330/selection/ae94b17d9a4c31cb8b8b32b5e855bebc16aaa6d99f564985973e8ff02dca8b49" :answer/id #uuid "90f2aee8-5099-55e5-8434-b5bdfed0f2d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135330/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a306d4d-6c50-5829-8ef7-d3229a2ce859" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135330/selection/583ed5a6da69542ecec5bee151e2915afa46c47d13c8442b64a6497084c99e78" :answer-field/choices ["q-135330/selection/d9419fe7cabdc7d4a05eed4347f4c93c371a5fc839025fe3b05d90b4f2cc11c3" "q-135330/selection/3b526d0871203a7fa20c2a891525c650a26e23eb2a93fea36737a1cf4d4423af" "q-135330/selection/583ed5a6da69542ecec5bee151e2915afa46c47d13c8442b64a6497084c99e78" "q-135330/selection/bf254af2a78e33a4bd565e51e6fc486096a404668e6dc60947f3560e2e649954" "q-135330/selection/ae94b17d9a4c31cb8b8b32b5e855bebc16aaa6d99f564985973e8ff02dca8b49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135330" :question/id #uuid "493b2715-cbc4-552a-b444-e7807620d6e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-135330" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.35 & 1 \\\\ 0.65 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $q$ is the steady-state vector of the stochastic matrix $P,$ what is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq & =q \\\\ Pq-q & =0 \\\\ Pq-Iq & =0 \\\\ (P-I)q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.35 & 1 \\\\ 0.65 & 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.65 & 1 \\\\ 0.65 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.65 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.65 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-0.65 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-0.65{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 65{x}_{1}-100{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 13{x}_{1}-20{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{20}{13}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20}{13}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20}{13}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{33}{13}{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =\\frac{13}{33}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20}{33} \\\\ \\frac{13}{33}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a-b=\\frac{20}{33}-\\frac{13}{33}=\\frac{7}{33}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-135330/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f53fa522-6d50-51d9-abdd-62735575a2d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135355/selection/4016fdcebd2706f02fec6751d03cdebb65c38e686a4c908928ff821b56632e4d" :answer/id #uuid "bed4e822-8907-5378-98ee-1e5f188dfd74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135355/selection/778e261ef33dc915e7aec5bb141e6ad4a26178c5b85f8771fbe1ce72fc0e00fb" :answer/id #uuid "a281f01a-da97-51f6-8eed-270aac899700" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135355/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "4e5b2ab7-0f38-555f-8755-3a8b4ce94fb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135355/selection/ff0685038436a148f4cbd816798fad7bc9dca49bd0c36c3225582ac51388eb1d" :answer/id #uuid "c0d6b486-5077-556b-9754-1541d9575e22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135355/selection/d59951cee3568817d4d77897aec24c04fc5c1a60c1051758780613d08e37caeb" :answer/id #uuid "6bccd713-85e7-5d4e-a554-cb07cb529eeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135355/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c26d446-a25a-5bf8-9909-7a8bf199311f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135355/selection/d59951cee3568817d4d77897aec24c04fc5c1a60c1051758780613d08e37caeb" :answer-field/choices ["q-135355/selection/4016fdcebd2706f02fec6751d03cdebb65c38e686a4c908928ff821b56632e4d" "q-135355/selection/778e261ef33dc915e7aec5bb141e6ad4a26178c5b85f8771fbe1ce72fc0e00fb" "q-135355/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-135355/selection/ff0685038436a148f4cbd816798fad7bc9dca49bd0c36c3225582ac51388eb1d" "q-135355/selection/d59951cee3568817d4d77897aec24c04fc5c1a60c1051758780613d08e37caeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135355" :question/id #uuid "b4c80da8-397f-5662-ba7f-3c2b3d84443d" :question/math-academy-id "q-135355" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.6 & 0.9 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.1\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $q$ is the steady-state vector of the stochastic matrix $P$ shown above, what is the value of $a+b-c?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq & =q \\\\ Pq-q & =0 \\\\ Pq-Iq & =0 \\\\ (P-I)q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.6 & 0.9 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.6 & 0.6 & 0.9 \\\\ 0.4 & -0.8 & 0 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & -0.9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.6 & 0.6 & 0.9 & 0 \\\\ 0.4 & -0.8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & -0.9 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=10{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=10{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:=10{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 6 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -9 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12 & -18 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-6{x}_{1}+6(\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3})+9{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{11}{2}{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{11} \\\\ \\frac{3}{11} \\\\ \\frac{2}{11}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b-c=\\frac{6}{11}+\\frac{3}{11}-\\frac{2}{11}=\\frac{7}{11}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135355/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84798595-cdd4-57bf-953f-0856b041b65f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135355"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135432/selection/3e1064098628ec53bad3b3af83ed06551a6f8b7b2fd6670eb40c10e4691c57ca" :answer/id #uuid "92d6b4aa-7bdd-5e79-806b-cbd42e4402d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52\\,500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135432/selection/c8b9cebda3eaa2f78b7e463b3cfdab27d2ea451ea76b854d351342bbb1e0b673" :answer/id #uuid "2fc88b31-2545-53e7-8d46-9806ded34741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37\\,500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135432/selection/a22ab1ef026d025376c1576ea3fa79feea443f69eda6dc935f5972fc0cb2f208" :answer/id #uuid "6550b82a-eafa-5999-b435-780ca8d5c0ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135432/selection/e2475d6a0d5fcc1630a2b114e8098ab669b74d2574dee2dadcff3ddf3e017eae" :answer/id #uuid "c4e56527-20e1-555c-8978-75aa597c72da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135432/selection/c14988d70cdd906b258c31e1fc3baca3fa11b2f3d83978b02a414e6388dcb73e" :answer/id #uuid "266e89ea-f009-5edc-afde-ef983f41dfce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42\\,500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135432/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "803dbf47-bd15-593e-a307-ee40b421c90b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135432/selection/e2475d6a0d5fcc1630a2b114e8098ab669b74d2574dee2dadcff3ddf3e017eae" :answer-field/choices ["q-135432/selection/3e1064098628ec53bad3b3af83ed06551a6f8b7b2fd6670eb40c10e4691c57ca" "q-135432/selection/c8b9cebda3eaa2f78b7e463b3cfdab27d2ea451ea76b854d351342bbb1e0b673" "q-135432/selection/a22ab1ef026d025376c1576ea3fa79feea443f69eda6dc935f5972fc0cb2f208" "q-135432/selection/e2475d6a0d5fcc1630a2b114e8098ab669b74d2574dee2dadcff3ddf3e017eae" "q-135432/selection/c14988d70cdd906b258c31e1fc3baca3fa11b2f3d83978b02a414e6388dcb73e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135432" :question/id #uuid "f64144f1-4784-509a-8280-15bc282eeef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-135432" :question/problem "A company processes and packages three types of rice: rice $A,$ rice $B,$ and rice $C.$ A study by the company's sales analysts demonstrates how consumer preference changes from one kind of rice to another year after year. The table below shows the results of this study.\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rice $A$** | **Rice $B$** | **Rice $C$** |\n| To: | **Rice $A$** | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| **Rice $B$** | $0.2$ | $0.7$ | $0.2$ |  |\n| **Rice $C$** | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.65$ |  |\n\nFor example, $20%$ of the people who preferred rice $B$ last year switched to rice $C$ this year.\n\nIf the company has $200\\,000$ customers and the listed probabilities remain constant over many years, how many customers will eventually purchase rice $B?$" :question/worked-solution "From the table, we get the corresponding stochastic matrix \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0.1 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.7 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.2 & 0.65\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $P$ contains only positive entries. So, the matrix $P$ is regular. \nAs a result, after many years, the distribution will eventually converge to the steady-state vector of $P,$ and this convergence does not depend on the initial state.\n\nRecall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq=q\\,⟹\\,(P-I)q=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0.1 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.7 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.2 & 0.65\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.5 & 0.1 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.2 & -0.3 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.2 & -0.35\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.5 & 0.1 & 0.15 & 0 \\\\ 0.2 & -0.3 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.2 & -0.35 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=10{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=100{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:=100{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & 1.5 & 0 \\\\ 20 & -30 & 20 & 0 \\\\ 30 & 20 & -35 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & 1.5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -26 & 26 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 26 & -26 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & 1.5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -26 & 26 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={x}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-5{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, after many years, $\\frac{2}{5}$ of the customers will consume rice $B.$ Therefore, the number of people who will eventually consume rice $B$ will be\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 200\\,000=80\\,000.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-135432/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84798595-cdd4-57bf-953f-0856b041b65f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135432"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141024/selection/33dee45065a895499539a367890d6dde98dee5fa0a2ccb4807198ad6fbb04c63" :answer/id #uuid "f1066c6d-cde9-5269-bde3-f99fe8189e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,040" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141024/selection/30977367a97b1d16deb59531a2ca213549cff7fe6b695e95386b7b46cc60f8a9" :answer/id #uuid "3f8806cc-31cc-57dc-b7d2-70e41a85781c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "680" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141024/selection/1289818130db4a91cf65c94aea980317a5cc0c0a60eda405e73cb9715e4aa767" :answer/id #uuid "12cbb84c-7ab3-5e5c-a2e4-2edcd3ff3a19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,360" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141024/selection/2e3ac8a9be268ab7b7c07f98cd54459f6b3b2f925f90387606bc9479a0d5dbfd" :answer/id #uuid "e2908d65-2456-531a-8708-48b21605757a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "340" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141024/selection/54f3bdde391c435fc1d46838a4cbe68503f3605046271aa4e817679e792a5865" :answer/id #uuid "5aec5c90-0af0-5d1a-b196-c1e27789708f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,700" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141024/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b4e2351-f2aa-5fa6-a595-16cc169555b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141024/selection/54f3bdde391c435fc1d46838a4cbe68503f3605046271aa4e817679e792a5865" :answer-field/choices ["q-141024/selection/33dee45065a895499539a367890d6dde98dee5fa0a2ccb4807198ad6fbb04c63" "q-141024/selection/30977367a97b1d16deb59531a2ca213549cff7fe6b695e95386b7b46cc60f8a9" "q-141024/selection/1289818130db4a91cf65c94aea980317a5cc0c0a60eda405e73cb9715e4aa767" "q-141024/selection/2e3ac8a9be268ab7b7c07f98cd54459f6b3b2f925f90387606bc9479a0d5dbfd" "q-141024/selection/54f3bdde391c435fc1d46838a4cbe68503f3605046271aa4e817679e792a5865"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141024" :question/id #uuid "a031dbeb-978c-5542-b4e9-e4e60f2dc984" :question/math-academy-id "q-141024" :question/problem "A study conducted on $3\\,400$ teenagers by the transportation department of a particular city reveals that teenagers' preference for the type of home-to-school transportation changes with time. The following table shows the results of this study.  \n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Bus** | **Bicycle** | **Electric Scooter ** |\n| To: | **Bus** | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0$ |\n| **Bicycle** | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ |  |\n| **Electric Scooter** | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ |  |\n\nFor example, $40%$ of teenagers who used to go to school by bus now go by bicycle.  \n\nHow many teenagers would eventually go to school on electric scooters if the listed probabilities remained constant over many years?" :question/worked-solution "From the table, we get the corresponding stochastic matrix \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.4 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.4 & 0.6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix ${P}^{2}$ contains only positive entries. So, the matrix $P$ is regular. \nAs a result, after many years, the distribution will eventually converge to the steady-state vector of $P,$ and this convergence does not depend on the initial state.\n\nRecall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq=q\\,⟹\\,(P-I)q=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.4 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.4 & 0.6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.8 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.4 & -0.6 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.4 & -0.4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.8 & 0.2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0.4 & -0.6 & 0.4 & 0 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.4 & -0.4 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=5{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{3})-{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3}+\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ 2{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{4}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, after many years, $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the teenagers will go to school in electric scooters. Therefore, the total number of teenagers in the city that will go to school in electric scooters will be\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\,400=1\\,700.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-141024/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84798595-cdd4-57bf-953f-0856b041b65f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141035/selection/bbd747b8490dd7bcbd3092b0ed2a9ea15c3da69bd480728252c6b1d0abe89b4b" :answer/id #uuid "832636af-5e32-5e8e-a70f-0899d4733c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "630" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141035/selection/582f5f4a49c608009627e9613c6d3c0b7ef49f7e381e7a6064e41f25c7d299cd" :answer/id #uuid "988496d8-e783-5faa-8afc-00a7da709fda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "540" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141035/selection/c934a131d434e7d3c931048e8a41560c3e62c804b2062f96ba5d40e9fb2d7c3b" :answer/id #uuid "c51165d8-9d04-581d-b131-d4615e6ea7b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "720" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141035/selection/fa2764e4d443b0fd1a8b9b79f38b985d2b576f72681c3b867c06cfeb24c839e4" :answer/id #uuid "54f07ad4-5fd7-52f2-bb37-ed138b81d121" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "360" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141035/selection/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" :answer/id #uuid "07cd4c8d-a940-5ddd-b100-55c57b972ce9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141035/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "94bb32e2-c8af-5d16-8c0a-d4734611d04c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141035/selection/fa2764e4d443b0fd1a8b9b79f38b985d2b576f72681c3b867c06cfeb24c839e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-141035/selection/bbd747b8490dd7bcbd3092b0ed2a9ea15c3da69bd480728252c6b1d0abe89b4b" "q-141035/selection/582f5f4a49c608009627e9613c6d3c0b7ef49f7e381e7a6064e41f25c7d299cd" "q-141035/selection/c934a131d434e7d3c931048e8a41560c3e62c804b2062f96ba5d40e9fb2d7c3b" "q-141035/selection/fa2764e4d443b0fd1a8b9b79f38b985d2b576f72681c3b867c06cfeb24c839e4" "q-141035/selection/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141035" :question/id #uuid "2a524bf3-7523-5a68-9c7e-5b4a3b2b91b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-141035" :question/problem "A study shows how the sports preferences of young people in a certain community vary from year to year. The following table shows the results of this study. \n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Baseball** | **Basketball** | **Football** |\n| To: | **Baseball** | $0.8$ | $0.2$ | $0$ |\n| **Basketball** | $0.1$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ |  |\n| **Football** | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ |  |\n\nFor example, $10%$ of people who used to prefer baseball now prefer football. \n\nGiven that $1\\,260$ young people were interviewed for the study and that the probabilities listed remain constant for many years, how many of those people will eventually prefer baseball?" :question/worked-solution "From the table, we get the corresponding stochastic matrix \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.6 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.2 & 0.8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix ${P}^{2}$ contains only positive entries. So, the matrix $P$ is regular. \nAs a result, after many years, the distribution will eventually converge to the steady-state vector of $P,$ and this convergence does not depend on the initial state.\n\nRecall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq=q\\,⟹\\,(P-I)q=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.6 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.2 & 0.8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.1 & -0.4 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.2 & -0.2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 & 0.2 & 0 \\\\ 0.1 & -0.4 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.2 & -0.2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=10{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:=10{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{3}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{7} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} \\\\ \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, after many years, $\\frac{2}{7}$ of the people will prefer baseball. Therefore, the number of people who will prefer baseball is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot 1\\,260=360\\,\\text{people}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-141035/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84798595-cdd4-57bf-953f-0856b041b65f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141035"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135344/selection/29648ef4e020fc43d1b46acbdbbedfd18f3de75ade3ca2e0ef505839d2f8c39b" :answer/id #uuid "3b72bb34-e9a9-598f-af83-fe4219b80009" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135344/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "0559f778-e830-5cea-bda4-fec7a3d10398" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135344/selection/7d601ef50c8431af674ed320eb7b90dc1e1bab1f3983928c9ae5edd90f9e5875" :answer/id #uuid "a362d0df-43f6-5cbd-877d-ecb47458173b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135344/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "52f3f8df-99ad-5c0d-845f-dd4c0ad54a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135344/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "cf98a9d9-03e2-55b0-b975-eea721940572" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135344/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7918654f-e285-59dc-b13b-635e418f5503" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135344/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-135344/selection/29648ef4e020fc43d1b46acbdbbedfd18f3de75ade3ca2e0ef505839d2f8c39b" "q-135344/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-135344/selection/7d601ef50c8431af674ed320eb7b90dc1e1bab1f3983928c9ae5edd90f9e5875" "q-135344/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-135344/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135344" :question/id #uuid "c6be156a-2b5e-5033-8af9-c73086a6bd49" :question/math-academy-id "q-135344" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.2 & 0.65 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $q$ is the steady-state vector of the stochastic matrix $P$ shown above, what is the value of $a+b-c?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq & =q \\\\ Pq-q & =0 \\\\ Pq-Iq & =0 \\\\ (P-I)q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n$$\nP-I=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.2 & 0.65 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & 0.25\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-0.6 & 0.2 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.3 & -0.8 & 0.65 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & -0.75\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)q=0$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.6 & 0.2 & 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0.3 & -0.8 & 0.65 & 0 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & -0.75 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=10{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:=10{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 0.5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 6.5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -7.5 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 0.5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -7 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 0.5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={x}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}+0.5{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b-c=\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135344/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84798595-cdd4-57bf-953f-0856b041b65f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135344"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9178"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/859a831dcc11fa6ffe430cc913fa46283d3231816429d3fea98219fe3417b746.png)\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $\\mathbf{q}$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\mathbf{q}$ is a stochastic vector\n\n- $P\\mathbf{q} = \\mathbf{q}$\n\n- $\\mathbf{q}$ is a steady-state vector of $P$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $\\mathbf{q}$ such that $P\\mathbf{q} = \\mathbf{q}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $\\mathbf{q}$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/a172ba62aed6c25fc1b40fdf70b1ae88a7e33d2f3341696783b96defd927b6be.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $\\mathbf{q}$ is a stochastic vector such that $P\\mathbf{q}=\\mathbf{q}.$ So, it's a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9179"] :question/problem "The table below describes how the customers of a particular electronics store feel about their next computer purchase.\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Laptop** | **Desktop** |\n| To: | **Laptop** | $0.9$ | $0.8$ |\n| **Desktop** | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |  |\n\nIt is found that $10 \\%$ of customers who currently use a laptop would choose a desktop on their next purchase, while $80 \\%$ of customers who currently use a desktop would choose a laptop on their next purchase. \n\nGiven that the store has $5\\,400$ customers, all of whom purchase a new computer every two years, how many customers would eventually own a desktop computer if the given probabilities remain constant over many two-year periods?" :question/worked-solution "From the table, we get the corresponding stochastic matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/1935c4960a48e2b446c2610b9edc2a160a5f45462494c72a90f139ea2d13cc34.png)\n\nNotice that $P$ contains only positive entries. So, the matrix $P$ is regular. As a result, after many two-year periods, the distribution will eventually converge to the unique steady-state vector of $P,$ and this convergence does not depend on the initial state.\n\nRecall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $\\mathbf{q}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq=q\\,⟹\\,(P-I)q=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/29b5a209bb27b24f165ee418326763d8fb24f83f2b3a767052c381aa8cd0e01c.png)\n\nSo, the matrix equation $(P-I)\\mathbf{q} = \\mathbf{0}$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.8 & 0 \\\\ 0.1 & -0.8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, $x_2$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=8{x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/0e8f620c3392dbb77b1353184e38eaf48b526aa82c502772a5582bd20c7f5aea.png)\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{2}+{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ 9{x}_{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur steady-state vector is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/2ed7b0fc7296b2b651909c7c15c73e253fc8a9f95fb037072228d5de6f838894.png)\n\nSo, ${\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{1}{9}}}$ of the $5\\,400$ customers would eventually own a desktop computer. Therefore, the total number of people who would eventually own a desktop computer is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{9} \\cdot 5\\,400 = 600.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9180"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/093de94431946cb83e7cc0523405989b7a23cc8d9677bdecdfba7aaf207fd62b.png)\n\nFind the steady-state vector $\\mathbf q$ of the stochastic matrix $P$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $\\mathbf{q}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pq & =q \\\\ Pq-q & =0 \\\\ Pq-Iq & =0 \\\\ (P-I)q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $P-I,$ we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/5ed2f76d9b2857134a5b2aa5781711f9625cabb46a9ca3c3d54aa31c32bb4dbe.png)\n\nThe matrix equation $(P-I)\\mathbf{q} = \\mathbf{0}$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.9 & 0.3 & 0.5 & 0 \\\\ 0.2 & -0.7 & 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.4 & -0.6 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=20{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=10{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:=20{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 6 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & 8 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}↔{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 6 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 14 & 8 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+9{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -57 & 19 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 57 & -19 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -57 & 19 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, $x_3$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\nx_2=\\dfrac{1}{3}x_3.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2x_1 -7\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}x_3\\right) + x_3 = 0 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_1 = \\dfrac{2}{3}x_3.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/9ae5533dc825d2d3d08ca7a54c50578e21dda8fad7988b9043baaad2a69368b7.png)\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{3}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ 2{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, our steady-state vector is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061943/assets/fd7775b5d982d0bc51e80417a70b67dbff0176afcc5ff9aec613947076201386.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
